# Build output and caches. .zig-cache alone is ~488 MB and rebuilds on
# demand; zig-out is the produced binary.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# Scratch data written by examples. Example 05 builds a data file and
# removes it, but a run killed mid-way leaves one behind.
_example*.bin
_p05*.bin
_probe*.bin

# Ring/Softanza engine artefacts
*.ringo
*.obj
*.pdb

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~

# Ring++ is an independent project. `.central/` is coordination state from
# the Softanza estate's harness -- an inbox, an outbox and a status page --
# which was tracked here and does not belong in a public Ring package.
# Ignored rather than merely deleted: the harness may write it again, and a
# regenerated file must not silently re-enter the history.
.central/

# Same reason: Central rewrites WHATS-NEXT.md with the estate's cross-repo
# plan (reference-design versions, the UI law, contracts) and instructions to
# open a mailbox under D:/GitHub/softanza. None of that is Ring++'s roadmap
# or a reader's business. Ring++'s own plan is docs/PHASE_PLAN.md.
WHATS-NEXT.md
